<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Hall of Mosses Trail — Hall of Mosses Trail</name><desc>The Hall of Mosses Trail in Washington’s Hoh Rain Forest packs tall old-growth trees, ferns and hanging moss into a short woodland loop. The maple grove is a particularly rich section, worth slowing down to see. The mapped walk includes the approach from the visitor area and the grove spur, about 1.6 km in total. Arrive early when possible: summer entry queues can outlast the walk. Roots, steps and short steep slopes make it unsuitable as a smooth wheelchair stroll.

